{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution","id":566455,"title":"Vampire 'Evolution'","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-24T08:50:00-07:00","id":566455,"title":"Vampire 'Evolution'","content":"Hi everyone! I have some brain food for you all!<br /> <br /> Along with some of my other questions, this one is potentially also scrubbish, if at least not weird.<br /> <br /> Awhile ago I had a character, originally started in Masquerade and transferred to Reqiuem (did not play 2E with him though), who was utterly power hungry. Not politically, but physically. He want power over everyone and everything. So, he diablerized as many enemies as he could (I always joked that he thought of Disciplines like they were Pokemon. Gotta catch 'em all!). There was a devotion he took (I don't remember if it was house ruled or if it was there normally) so that his aura did not give this away (I think normally it was black,veiny lines in the aura). It did take a huge toll on his psyche, would be very paranoid at times/act irrationally as some of the souls he devoured would linger. Sadly, the game was ended as I had to move away but I was in the process of trying to create him into something more. (OOC, him also turning into a demon/werewolf/mage powers/etc etc. Anything that he could). Now, originally what my plan was, was to somehow get into the Lucifuge. It never states that only humans may join them (actually states that the leader is most likely not human), and it gives him access to demons. He would go through demon after demon until he found what he was after. Either someway to 'evolve' into one, or find a way to infiltrate a mage tower. I hadn't worked out a way for the whole werewolf thing yet, and I have no experience with any of the others (very little in anything but vampire and hunter really). If he was able to obtain what he wanted, he would have the benefits of all, as well as their weaknesses. This is assuming, of course, that everyone/thing he has/had pissed off doesn't manage to kill him first.<br /> <br /> So, I guess my question is, is there a way for a vampire to 'evolve/transform' into a demon/werewolf and somehow make his way to a mage tower (or anything else for that matter.)? It just happened to come across my mind again and figured I would ask those a lot more knowledgable than myself <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 06-24-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:06:17-07:00","id":566490,"title":"","content":"Not without losing the vampire template. NWoD doesn't allow mixing of major templates, so if you wanted to do something like this it would be homebrew territory.<br /> <br /> Also this Devotion your old character had sounds like one of the bloodline abilities of a bloodline called the En. That's the only &quot;canon&quot; means of hiding diablerie stains that I can remember, though it may well have been a homebrew Devotion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:13:42-07:00","id":566552,"title":"","content":"Ah, alas I didn't think so.<br /> <br /> Although would it of been possible for one to enter the Lucifuge and still retain the vampire template? Since it only really translates, at least on paper, as a couple of merit points.<br /> <br /> As for the 'En', he was definitely not that. So must of been homebrew. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Addition:<br /> <br /> So, getting the wheels turning. IF you were to allow someone to obtain such desires, how would you go about it? I haven't been able to think of anything else other than enslaving demons (at least for finding this information. I feel if anything would know how, it would be them. But then again, with next to no experience with Demon, I keep thinking of Supernatural's Crossroad demons.)<br /> <br /> For Mage, maybe possessing someone the same time that they are first Awakened?<br /> For a werewolf, maybe if he were embraced before your first transformation? Or maybe during it? But what about if you already are a vampire..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":".  More food for thought. 06-24-2015, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:35:50-07:00","id":566591,"title":"","content":"If you're embraced before the first change it just never happens. You need to be alive to shift.<br /> <br /> I think your best bet is to make questionable deals with obscenely powerful entities. An archmage or godlike spirit could probably alter you in such a manner, if they so wished.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:42:46-07:00","id":566611,"title":"","content":"There was a charatcer back in OWoD who did something like this, becomming some wierd Mage-Werewolf-Vampire thingie.<br /> I think he ended up as an ashtray in the Underworld, though. Might wanna check him out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T09:46:52-07:00","id":566617,"title":"","content":"There is a vampire, Eddie Vines, who is also possessed by a demon. I don't think I'd want a vampire to <i>become </i>a demon, since then they'd be unplayable. But a vampire can learn the standard occult workings that allow people to theoretically control demons, anyone can. If you want a tie in to the Lucifuge you can give them a +2 bonus to dice pools to dealing with demons in a demonologist fashion but I wouldn't allow them to get the endowments, normally, as the vampirism sort of wipes out the demonic vestiges in them.<br /> <br /> A werewolf who is embraced before their First Change is a vampire. They might have access to the dead wolves bloodline but they're never going to be a werewolf again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 06-24-2015, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:16:04-07:00","id":566637,"title":"","content":"Going by the materials presented in the book, not directly no. If someone wanted to play a character with that as their long term agenda, and I felt they were actually going to stick with the game, I'd probably run them through a Golconda quest that either allow them to evolve into a lesser demon or alternatively, become a normal human again, and then Awaken. They would in the course of gameplay be stricken with lycanthropy and get some of the benefits of being a werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:25:32-07:00","id":566643,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all of the replies!<br /> <br /> I was thinking Golconda might have something to do with it as well at one point.<br /> <br /> Krobeles, any idea on what his name was?<br /> <br /> Also, why would a demon/vampire be unplayable? (I'm actually not sure why. Like I said earlier, no experience with Demon)<br /> Also, would being a vamps blood make them ineligible for Lucifuge endowments? The only reason I ask is because it hints that the leader might be a vampire already. If not, then its most likely not human at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T10:28:37-07:00","id":566666,"title":"","content":"Character's Name was Samuel Haight... also known as &quot;<i><b>The Skinner</b></i>&quot;.<br /> If you PM me your email I can send you his official PDF.<br /> He did indeed become a Wraithly Ashtray at the end.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","user":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","date":". 06-24-2015, 03:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T11:05:30-07:00","id":566701,"title":"","content":"Demons, as in from Demon the Descent, aren't traditional demons. They're creations of the God Machine that have gone AWOL. But a traditional demon wouldn't really be something you'd want to play because it's a one note kind of thing. It spreads vice, that's it. It has no sense of personal fulfillment and no reason to do anything but spread vice. Things like that make for poor character concepts because there's no personal development beyond the obtaining of new malpraxes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T06:25:25-07:00","id":567803,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I can see why a lot of people wouldn't want to play that. Although for this purposes it could prove to be very interesting. <br /> <br /> Say if the vampire did have to reach Golcanda (which if I remember correctly, it's like, Monk level kindness). Reaches it then is transformed, well, maybe not completely transformed (maybe more like cursed. Like some sort of half-blooded demon), and he has to fight off the temptations. Could be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T06:34:30-07:00","id":567809,"title":"","content":"A lucifuge vampire may be possible, but that seems like something more possible in the opposite order- a lucifuge getting embraced.<br /> <br /> However, since the situation seems to be that when a lucifuge dies another lucifuge is called, one could make the point that any template that actually requires dying makes one a former lucifuge.<br /> <br /> However, the ordo dracul are going to get a &quot;coil of the zirnitra&quot; for reclaiming lost mortal supernatural abilities, so a storyteller might allow you to use castigations through that coil, detailed <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1_J83T-t9g-87pvtUTKCZIJ2QQzCTOzUclkWJjsvb814/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> As for a vampire becoming a demon, sort of. First step, die. Second step, leave a ghost. Third step, have the ghost turn into a demon, as outlined in Inferno. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T06:43:42-07:00","id":567813,"title":"","content":"Hmm, fair point with the Lucifuge thing. Who's to say they weren't one before they were embraced. It just happened to be a very traumatic one and suffered amnesia or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> As for the demon thing, a very risky first step. But in follow-up, could said Demon repossess your 'corpse'? So long as you weren't ashed. Or, what if you used Astral Projection or potentially some other discipline/sorcery that forces you out of your body?<br /> <br /> Following this method. For Mage, what would happen if you were in current possession of a mortal who is about to become Awakened? Not so much in total control, but just lurking in the background of their mind. Hoping to hitch a ride with them (either would have to be incredibly lucky or find some method of picking them out from the public. Speaking of which, is there anyway to tell?).<br /> <br /> Also Elfive, so you need to be alive in order to go through the first change. What about if you are a ghoul? Would that have any effect?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T06:57:42-07:00","id":567836,"title":"","content":"As an additional side topic. If you could mix any of the major templates, which would you choose? It doesn't necessarily need to become a super powerhouse monster. It could just be because of the utility of one over another.<br /> <br /> Example, the one I mentioned above I mainly wanted him to get access to mage powers so he can, essentially, become completely self reliant and no longer need to hunt (being able to manifest creatures with blood.. If I remember correctly). There was also the added benefit of he could make himself the best safe-haven using a mixture of powers (I can't remember them all, but you could essentially make a small pouch a massive area that can sustain life). Come to thing of it, he would kind of become a Genie... I like it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:14:33-07:00","id":567871,"title":"","content":"This Makes me think he's trying too became an Alpha predator... He's going though Golconda Via becoming an Incarnate ala Beast.<br /> I'd Never let a Player Actually succeed, but i'd definately have them as an Antagonist.<br /> Drinking an Abyssal Diablerising it, Consuming the essence of Urtha (Probably an entire pack and its Totem), Capturing and drawing the Divine Fire (Capturing and Torturing a Promethean) into oneself and using that as a Catalyst for becoming something New.... You'd have too Leave out the GM Demons... as i don't see them synegysing well with the other powers, Infernal powers on the other hand, Mortal can learn some Tricks from them if i remember anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:27:01-07:00","id":567893,"title":"","content":"Ya, essentially the idea was once he got powerful enough, he would just kind of stop being around. If he managed to do what I said above (the self-sufficient bag-home thing), he would simply hide in there until something disturbed him. The more and more I think about it, he really would be like a Genie, just one that grants death instead of wishes. Because really, he didn't care for much other than a few individuals.. And Texas. His goal was to destroy Texas. I can't remember why, he just had a deep hatred for it. <br /> <br /> Those are all fantastic ideas. Eat everything to absorb them and their powers. What about Mage though? I liked the idea of trying to infiltrate one of the towers somehow. Or even more interesting, creating his own!! But then the question arises, how does one get their?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:30:35-07:00","id":567895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution?p=567871#post567871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd Never let a Player Actually succeed</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree but with an implicit &quot;except <i>right</i> at the end of a chronicle&quot; in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:37:59-07:00","id":567916,"title":"","content":"There are revenants, in first edition ghosts with a numina to possess their own bodies, in second edition it would probably be a manifestation effect.<br /> <br /> Possessing someone else's corpse is possible with intruder, again a numina in first edition but probably a manifestation in second edition.<br /> <br /> There are also bhuta, ghosts who possess other people killing them, and only able to replenish their essence through vampirism and cannibalism. <br /> <br /> And to answer your question about the first change, minor templates may or may not be trumped. So it's up to the storyteller if say a wolf-blood possessed by a demon or given vampire blood would stay a wolf-blood or become one of the possessed or a ghoul. Major templates always trump minor templates. So a ghoul who visits a watchtower or gets chosen by Luna to become a werewolf will be a former ghoul. <br /> <br /> In second edition, they're allowing some templates to leave marks though. A wolf-blooded turned into another supernatural will retain their tell but lose any wolf-blooded merits they might have had for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T07:56:05-07:00","id":567932,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Interesting. And yes, I agree. Right at the end of a chronicle. Like I said, he was to essentially disappear shortly afterwards. Having obtained his goals, he no longer cares about the world.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of the 'marks'. Something that says, &quot;Yes, I used to be -this-&quot;. Making weird hybrids. I like the idea. (question, there were Liches before right? Mages who essentially became vampires? Or at least some sort of undead creature but retained their mage powers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:14:01-07:00","id":567952,"title":"","content":"I guess a mage who artificially prolongs their life with death magic could do so by becoming some sort of undead. (one more for the potential vampire origin pile, perhaps?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T08:25:48-07:00","id":567982,"title":"","content":"Ya, that's what I was thinking. Okay, so still following this origin method. Still making hybrids. Could a mage join a Hunter Conspiracy? Would those templates interfere with each other or would it be fine? (I can see anything + hunter template mixing well since it essentially just adds more merits, not another resource pool).<br /> <br /> I'm thinking, following the new Ordo merits (which all seem pretty fantastic), it makes a lot of this possible. Providing it is all written in the origin story. A Mage who was embraced, joins the order has he hears that they have methods of regaining parts of your mortal life. The ability to relearn what one has lost so long ago. It's turning somewhat poetic from what it original was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:09:42-07:00","id":568108,"title":"","content":"Hunter is not a Template. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:14:58-07:00","id":568116,"title":"","content":"That's what I thought! So there is at least one Hybrid option with would work, so long as the in-game politics don't interfere too much. =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T10:50:09-07:00","id":568142,"title":"","content":"Some of the powers available to hunter Conspiracies would probably stop working if the hunter became a vampire, but a vampire from TFV could totally keep using their Advanced Armory, and the Cheiron Group might be perfectly willing to experiment with &quot;improving&quot; a recently embraced employee. After all, the rights of an undead, bloodsucking monster are kind of a legal gray area, and once you're a corpse TCG can probably own you lock, stock, and barrel. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:03:05-07:00","id":568648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution#post566455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I guess my question is, is there a way for a vampire to 'evolve/transform' into a demon/werewolf and somehow make his way to a mage tower (or anything else for that matter.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sightless Mother from Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners is a canonical example of a vampire &quot;evolving&quot; into another kind of powerful being (if you can call it &quot;evolving&quot;). She was killed and became a ghost whose anchor is Cruac. She knows all Cruac rituals and instantly travel to anyone who knows Cruac. She didn't need to feed as a ghost and gained 3 essence per hour from worshipers invoking her name.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Ancient Horrors&quot; section of Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners is a great resource for ideas about uber-vamps; in fact the whole book is great, I highly recommend it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:03:13-07:00","id":568649,"title":"","content":"Valkyrie equipment doesn't work without a microchip, which if memory serves stops working when the hunter dies, it's also rumoured to have a tracking function, so if I were a former valkyrie vampire I'd start digging...<br /> <br /> And the cheiron thing is canon actually, vampire and witch informants have been paid with thaumatech augmentation according to C&amp;C.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T19:12:56-07:00","id":568659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krzyzstof</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution?p=568116#post568116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I thought! So there is at least one Hybrid option with would work, so long as the in-game politics don't interfere too much. =D</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No reason a vampire couldn't work with Aegis Kai Doru; they're focused on Werewolves and Mages, and a vampire could probably use their mystic relics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T06:54:02-07:00","id":569158,"title":"","content":"Ya, I was always curious about the supernatural in Hunter Conspiracies. Like some of you mentioned, it seems like it would fit (thinking along the lines of Supernatural; if you're useful and do more good than harm, we won't kill you).<br /> <br /> StSword, really? I don't remember that. Well that makes it a little bit more difficult. <br /> <br /> Vyrkolash, I shall have to check that out!<br /> <br /> CatDoom, like I mentioned above. It seems like some groups would like the supernatural to join their ranks. If not because they trust them, because they can run experiments on hopefully a willing subject.<br /> <br /> The only one I really thought would of been difficult/taboo (before learning about the TFV chips not working in an undead host (although that means wolves/mages could still use them)), was the Malleus Maleficarum. Well, at least for anything that is fairly obviously not normal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:17:23-07:00","id":569168,"title":"","content":"Honestly, while crossing templates is a no-no, I think that new Coil of Sorcery is fine for this concept. There's plenty enough of stealing other supernatural powers associated with it, and the entire concept of vampire evolution is the basis of the Ordo Dracul's philosophy. The OP's concept is literally what the Ordo Dracul is made for.<br /> <br /> In short? Just wait until the <i>Secrets of the Covenant </i>book comes out with everything you want for this vampire without bothering the ST with crazy house rules and crossovers. If you want a bit more magic? Then steal some sorcery from the Lance or Crone, especially if the ST allows the Themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:24:55-07:00","id":569183,"title":"","content":"Ya, I was looking at that and it looks very promising.<br /> <br /> In all honesty though, this was from an old character of mine so no ST harassing or house rule frenzy here. It's just food for thought. The thought crossed my mind as to how, if possible, a vampire could achieve something along this line (at least getting Mage powers. That was the main one for him). It's more of just brain food as to how he would accomplish this. It was mentioned that devouring the souls of those whom you wish to emulate is an interesting idea. Would take quite a long time, and the effects of eating them would be interesting to play through. Mage was what, like a super high wasn't it? Werewolf caused a frenzy-like state if I remember. Don't know about any of the others. Or, like I mentioned for Mage. Develop some way of finding those whom have not awakened yet, somehow get into their brain without taking over, and tag along when it happens.<br /> <br /> But like I said, it's just brain food and not actual gameplay (at least for now!)<br /> <br /> <br /> Addition: Yes, he was with the Ordo and it was from them that I kind of got the idea. All about improving oneself. He took it a different way and wanting to try to gain the benefits of others. Wanting to experience what they do. What are these towers? How do Werewolves function? How can these mortals call upon Demons and what seems to be the powers of Gods! I must find out how they do this! Something along those lines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 06-26-2015, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T08:30:58-07:00","id":569232,"title":"","content":"Canonically there are two disciplines which allow vampires access to spirit or ghost numina, which can add interesting powers to a vampire's repertoire. Level 5 of the Blood Tenebrous discipline from Book of Spirits lets a vampire take a spirit into himself and become a sort of vampire/spirit hybrid with access to the powers of both. Level 5 of the Dracolescue (I think that's the name) bloodline's signature discipline (from the Ordo Dracul book) lets a vampire do the same with a ghost.<br /> <br /> In terms of homebrew options; I could also see an Ordo vampire gaining aspects of spirits or ghosts as a result of experiments in the right kinds of wyrm's nests. The merit for feeding on other mystical beings (I think it's &quot;Unnatural Affinity&quot;) could be applied to spirit loci or ghostly anchors. That would form the basis for turning essence into vitae. New merits for Loci (1-5 dots), and/or Anchors (1-5 dots) could be taken to represent an ability to draw sustenance from those sources. Mechanically it would work kind of like a feeding ground merit by adding to a starting vitae roll, and thematically it would represent the vampires growing affinity for spirit and/or ghost essence. Dots in Loci would just represent the strength of the locus the vampire is feeding on, but dots in Anchors should each represent a single anchor for the vampire (like the touchstones merit).<br /> <br /> I'd also develop a devotion based on Twilight Projection (TP) so as to interact with ephemeral beings. Dots in Vigor, Celerity, and Resilience could be used to grant the vampire's twilight form stats for Power, Finesse, and Resistance. Alternatively, combining TP with Level 5 of Protean could allow a vampire to transform into an ephemeral being and enter a twilight state physically rather than mentally. Or, an Acolyte who knows rites which affect spirits and/or ghosts could substitute dots in Cruac for TP to make similar devotions.<br /> <br /> Then I'd take the &quot;Unnatural Affinity&quot; merit for ghosts and/or spirits. That would form the basis for turning their essence into vitae and for &quot;diablerizing&quot; them. On a mechanical level this would mean trading humanity points for numina, and possibly using spirit influences as the basis for entirely new disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6617-vyrkolash","name":"Vyrkolash","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T23:42:48-07:00","id":569996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution?p=568649#post568649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Valkyrie equipment doesn't work without a microchip, which if memory serves stops working when the hunter dies, it's also rumoured to have a tracking function, so if I were a former valkyrie vampire I'd start digging...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, I forgot about that. I think it's been described as an RFID chip... in principle I don't think it would be too difficult to replicate, if you have the budget and someone with the knowhow. Then again, if it's capable of terminating itself when the host dies, it could probably send some kind of kill signal to the equipment as well, assuming that TFV is more worried about someone else getting their tech than they are about losing valuable equipment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 06-27-2015, 02:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T14:13:53-07:00","id":570571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/566455-vampire-evolution?p=567871#post567871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This Makes me think he's trying too became an Alpha predator... He's going though Golconda Via becoming an Incarnate ala Beast.<br /> I'd Never let a Player Actually succeed, but i'd definately have them as an Antagonist.<br /> Drinking an Abyssal Diablerising it, Consuming the essence of Urtha (Probably an entire pack and its Totem), Capturing and drawing the Divine Fire (Capturing and Torturing a Promethean) into oneself and using that as a Catalyst for becoming something New.... You'd have too Leave out the GM Demons... as i don't see them synegysing well with the other powers, Infernal powers on the other hand, Mortal can learn some Tricks from them if i remember anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the point, I think. Someone who did just one of those things starts to became something \u201cnew\u201d and is not longer a Vampire. I think you have to ask, why the player wants to do so. If the answer is \u201cmore power\u201d, show him how to get more power in the framework of Vampire. If the answer is, he just like crossover, it's easy as pie. There are a lot of ways to crossover. For example, start with a Gangrel character in a Werewolf Pack. Or a Demon, with Vampire-like Powers and a stolen Vampire Identity (there are actual some Vampires I can imagine, that they are in fact Demons, Beasts or something stranger, did you ever wonder, why some of the most popular Vampires claim to be of no Clan and have no sire? Just think abut it!). If someone like to play something really strange, look at Beast. I think Beast (in spite of all it's weak points) could bring the answer of a lot of those questions. We know, the most WoD Monsters bare a kind of Beast (Werewolfs and Vampires are just the most obvious). I think it is possible, that a person who starts to combined different kinds of Beasts could finally unleash a primordial Terror and became a Beast (in the sens of one of the begotten). He may, or may not keep the powers of his old template. I think I would not keep the Vampire/Werewolf-tamplate but keep some features and weakness to remind this new Alpha what he once was.<br /> <br /> The Demon Question is a special one, because the GM-Demons are special creatures. To keep it short, the source of their Powers are mainly that they can remember the back doors of Physics and Metaphysics. I find the question interesting what would happen, if some other Creature get this knowledge. The Problem is, I am sure, that the GM will send destroyer angles to everyone who has this knowledge beside its own agents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2195-sethos","name":"Sethos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}